It seems that the WebSocket connection issue is likely due to the Nginx configuration. You need to ensure that the WebSocket upgrade headers are correctly set. In your Nginx configuration, you have the following lines, which are correct for handling WebSocket connections:

```nginx
proxy_http_version 1.1;
proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
```

However, you should also ensure that the location block for `/_stcore/stream/` is correctly set up to handle WebSocket connections. Make sure that the upstream server (your Streamlit app) is reachable from Nginx. You might also want to check if the WebSocket connection is being redirected or blocked by any other rules in your Nginx configuration. If the endpoint is returning a 301 status, it indicates a redirection issue, which could be due to incorrect path handling. Please verify that the paths are correctly configured and that the Streamlit app is accessible directly via the specified IP and port. If you continue to face issues, consider checking the Nginx logs for more detailed error messages.
